##Code Organization
- Group every new function into a #region / #endregion block by responsibility, such as #region Initialization, #region - - Public API, #region Animation, or #region Private Helpers.
- Add new functions to an existing matching region.
- Create a new clearly named region only when no matching region exists.
- Do not nest regions.
- Keep one responsibility per region.

##Component References
- Avoid using GetComponent, GetComponentInChildren, GetComponentInParent, or similar runtime component lookups.
- Avoid using AddComponent to construct dependencies dynamically.
- Prefer explicit [SerializeField] references assigned in the Unity Inspector.
- Validate required references during Initialize(...) when appropriate.

##Fail fast rule
- Avoid ensure() functions or return if a nullable object is null
- Make sure to fail as early as possible when needed